July 30th, 2005

    * I have successfully developed the more command. It works (mostly)
      I need to fix the line reading and changing stuff... but I think
      I know what the problem is. The simul_efun file_lines.c that I coded
      today as well is probably the source. It reades a file and splits it by
      seeing how many "\n"s are in the file... which doesn't work because often
      files have "\n" in a write() statement and therefore imaginary lines are
      added to the output. I've also started work on a tail command. It seems to 
      work as of now, but it also relies on file_lines and so gets inaccurate 
      readings. perhaps recommend making tail and more simul_efuns one day! well.. 
      that's all for now... I'm tired... *yawn* it's about 1:30AM.. so... off to bed.
   
    * Ok, back on track here; I've just finished writing and testing the
      (simple) save command. I'm going to be updating more and tail to make
      the default number of lines as 20, not 25. Also, I'll be looking at a
      simple nuke command.

    * More and tail are updated now. I'm working on adding a new simul_efun
      called user_exists. It basically checks to see if there is a user
      data file in /data/users/N/NAME.o ... pretty simple

    * Whee! tail() and more() are now simul_efuns. As soon as Tac fixes
      the problem with the simul_efuns, both commands should work fine.
      Also, so should user_exists! Now I think I'm going to code a
      log command to quickly tail the log specified (and if no log,
      just tail compile)

